      "message": "[ This is for a preexisting issue that isn\u0027t new with this CL... ]\n\nWhile you\u0027re at it, can you add a type annotation to require a true `bool` for `desiredpresence` arg?\n\nThat or add a defensive `desiredpresence \u003d bool(desiredpresence)` line at the beginning of the function.\n\nIt\u0027s not unusual for Python code to assume a boolean arg will simply be evaluated in a boolean context and doesn\u0027t need to be a true `bool`.  Since the current implementation would quietly accept that (but with unintended behavior), best to either force an error (type annotation, *if* that\u0027s truly enforced), or simply handle it (run it through `bool()`).",
